# The lander's hands on Workshop (#83m6zw8, #nvq0tc8): one pass of `loom push` (cmd/loom/push.go, package lander),
# which builds any block the queue opened, then fast-forwards the target branch (push.conf's branch, main unless it
# names another) to each landing order's exact tested sha with the lander key (Host github-lander). Run by
# loom-pusher.timer every 30 s. A pass that holds an order (GitHub's rules or the key refused it, or git failed) exits
# 1, so the unit reads failed until a pass lands or has nothing to hold.
#
# Nobody copies this file. `loom push install` writes it and its timer into ~/.config/systemd/user and reloads systemd,
# and the updater's hook ~/.loom/updated.d/60-push runs that after every release while ~/.loom/push.conf exists, so
# the units travel with the release. Install never enables or starts the timer: landing is Kirk's call,
#
#   systemctl --user enable --now loom-pusher.timer      (enable, so a reboot keeps it: cutover.sh on)
#   systemctl --user disable --now loom-pusher.timer     (cutover.sh off)
#
# Reads ~/.loom/push.conf (branch, queue, repository, state, secret; lander/config.go), the token secret
# (~/.loom/token-secret) each call mints a ten-minute coordinator token from, and the lander's bare clone
# ~/loom-lander/adamic.git, whose origin is git@github-lander:system-inc/adamic.git. One pass at a time:
# ~/loom-lander/state/lock.
[Unit]
Description=Loom pusher: landing orders to adamic's target branch, fast-forward only, with the lander key

[Service]
Type=oneshot
Environment=PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
ExecStart=%h/.loom/bin/loom push
StandardOutput=append:%h/loom-lander/pusher.log
StandardError=append:%h/loom-lander/pusher.log
TimeoutStartSec=600
